SFML DRM: drop the DRM master when the DRM context is cleaned up

The frontend closes its window to start a game and makes a new one when the
game ends. On an Intel Ironlake the Mesa leaves descriptors of /dev/dri/card0
open after eglTerminate() and gbm_device_destroy(), so the process stays the
master of the screen even after SFML closes its descriptor. The emulator
cannot take the screen ("Error when switching mode", it exits at once) and
the frontend, when it makes its window again, dies with "Failed to set mode:
Permission denied". drmDropMaster() on the descriptor before closing it
releases the master for every copy of it.

Closing the descriptor already drops the master where nothing is left open
(amdgpu, radeon), so there the call changes nothing.

diff --git a/extlibs/SFML/src/SFML/Window/DRM/DRMContext.cpp b/extlibs/SFML/src/SFML/Window/DRM/DRMContext.cpp
--- a/extlibs/SFML/src/SFML/Window/DRM/DRMContext.cpp
+++ b/extlibs/SFML/src/SFML/Window/DRM/DRMContext.cpp
@@ -122,6 +122,13 @@
     gbm_device_destroy(gbmDevice);
     gbmDevice = nullptr;
 
+    // The Mesa of the Intel Ironlake keeps descriptors of the card open after
+    // eglTerminate and gbm_device_destroy, so the process stays the master of
+    // the screen even after close(): the emulator the frontend starts next
+    // fails to set its mode, and the frontend itself cannot take the screen
+    // back when it makes its window again. The master goes first.
+    drmDropMaster(drmNode.fileDescriptor);
+
     close(drmNode.fileDescriptor);
 
     drmNode.fileDescriptor = -1;
